  tags$h3("Explore the map"),
  tags$ol(
    tags$li("Choose a species and switch between reported observations and climate suitability."),
    tags$li("For suitability, choose the baseline, future projection or climate-model disagreement."),
    tags$li("Use Map options to find a location and adjust opacity to reveal the satellite imagery.")),
  tags$h3("What the colours mean"),
  p("Pale rose to burgundy shows increasing modelled climate suitability on a fixed 0–1 scale. It does not estimate the probability of arrival or damage. Scores are not comparable risk levels across species; a low score does not establish that a location is safe."),
  p("The 2.5-arc-minute climate grid supports regional exploration, not stand-level assessment. Zooming in reveals the grid cells without adding finer climate information."),
  p("Mapped inland lakes are excluded from the climate display and remain transparent; they are not assigned zero suitability. The generalized Natural Earth lake mask does not include every small waterbody. Shorelines are approximate. Climate suitability does not establish forest or host-tree presence."),
  tags$details(tags$summary("Reported observations"),
    p("Live GBIF human observations are retrieved for each species. Museum specimens are excluded. Record coverage varies by species, and density reflects reporting effort rather than abundance. No records does not establish absence."),
    p("EAB and MPB use worldwide records across all years. OPM uses a European search region and the current year plus four preceding calendar years. A disputed German MPB record is excluded after review."),
    p("The interactive map retrieves up to 3,000 records, with a short time budget. It may show fewer if GBIF is slow. This is a browsing subset, not a representative sample. OPM retrieval prioritizes recent years. Successful results are reused for up to one hour within a running app process; Refresh records requests an update. If that update fails, previously retrieved records may remain visible. Individual points link to the original GBIF record.")),
  tags$details(tags$summary("Models and climate scenarios"),
    p("MaxEnt relates occurrence locations to climate conditions, then projects those relationships across Sweden. These are experimental models; Swedish predictive accuracy has not been established."),
    p("Baseline: provisional CRU-derived climatology for 2001–2020 at 2.5 arc minutes."),
    p("Future: 2041–2060 under SSP2-4.5, using the cellwise median of projections from EC-Earth3-Veg, MPI-ESM1-2-HR and MRI-ESM2-0."),
    p("Baseline preparation: monthly CRU-TS 4.09 data downscaled and bias-corrected using WorldClim 2.1. Each calendar month is averaged over 2001–2020; bioclimatic predictors are then calculated from this mean seasonal cycle."),
    p("The baseline QC procedure screens for incomplete inputs, monthly minimum temperature exceeding maximum temperature, negative precipitation and a precautionary constant-temperature reference pattern. This is quality screening, not independent validation of the climate data."),
    p("Future inputs: WorldClim-downscaled and bias-corrected CMIP6 bioclimatic layers at 2.5 arc minutes. The three pest-model projections are clamped before calculating their cellwise median and maximum-minus-minimum spread. The future inputs are not re-based to the custom 2001–2020 baseline in the projection script; baseline–future differences can therefore reflect climate-product differences as well as projected change."),
    p(tags$a("Historical monthly data and source citations", href = "https://www.worldclim.org/data/monthlywth.html", target = "_blank", rel = "noopener noreferrer"), " · ",
      tags$a("WorldClim CMIP6 data", href = "https://www.worldclim.org/data/cmip6/cmip6climate.html", target = "_blank", rel = "noopener noreferrer")),
    p("The blue disagreement layer is the maximum minus minimum suitability across the three climate models. It is not a confidence interval or total model uncertainty."),
    p("Research comparison switches between 200 km and 500 km background definitions. This assesses sensitivity to background choice; it is not a confidence interval.")),
  tags$details(tags$summary("Model evidence and technical details"),
    p("Choose a species below to view its beta model specification and limitations."),
    lapply(names(beta_model_specs), function(species)
      tags$details(tags$summary(species_common_names[[species]]), model_documentation(species)))),
  tags$details(tags$summary("Scientific references"),
    p("Studies consulted during model development. InvaSkog fits its own MaxEnt models; the maps are not reproductions of these studies and have not been validated by their authors."),
    tags$ul(
      tags$li(strong("Emerald ash borer — "), "Rossi, J.-P., Mouttet, R., Rousse, P. & Streito, J.-C. (2024). ",
        tags$a("Modelling the potential range of Agrilus planipennis in Europe according to current and future climate conditions.", href = "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tfp.2024.100559", target = "_blank", rel = "noopener noreferrer"),
        " Trees, Forests and People, 100559.",
        p(class = "small-note", "Context for climate-based range modelling of EAB in Europe. The study uses an ensemble approach; InvaSkog uses its own occurrence data, predictor subset and MaxEnt settings.")),
      tags$li(strong("Oak processionary moth — "), "Godefroid, M., Meurisse, N., Groenen, F., Kerdelhué, C. & Rossi, J.-P. (2020). ",
        tags$a("Current and future distribution of the invasive oak processionary moth.", href = "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10530-019-02108-4", target = "_blank", rel = "noopener noreferrer"),
        " Biological Invasions, 22, 523–534.",
        p(class = "small-note", "The CLIM2 predictor set informed the OPM selection: BIO5, BIO6, BIO16 and BIO17. InvaSkog uses a different climate baseline and its own fitted models.")),
      tags$li(strong("Mountain pine beetle — "), "Bentz, B. J., Jönsson, A. M., Schroeder, M., Weed, A., Wilcke, R. A. I. & Larsson, K. (2019). ",
        tags$a("Ips typographus and Dendroctonus ponderosae Models Project Thermal Suitability for Intra- and Inter-Continental Establishment in a Changing Climate.", href = "https://doi.org/10.3389/ffgc.2019.00001", target = "_blank", rel = "noopener noreferrer"),
        " Frontiers in Forests and Global Change, 2, 1.",
        p(class = "small-note", "Biological context for temperature-dependent development and cold survival. This is a mechanistic modelling study; InvaSkog does not implement its physiological models.")))),
  tags$h3("Species information"),
  p("The species cards provide an adult reference photo and a link to EPPO for further information and photographs. InvaSkog focuses on preparedness and map exploration.")
)
